<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LeisureNet raises half yr share, no div.</title>
<headline>LeisureNet raises half yr share, no div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		    (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr - headline (cts)     11.1    vs   8.8</p>
<p>    Shr - weighted avg (cts) 11.2    vs   8.8</p>
<p>    Net earnings		 12.35   vs   6.59</p>
<p>    Before tax		   19.46   vs  10.39</p>
<p>    Tax			     7.06   vs   3.79</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 4.68   vs   2.80</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	 0.81   vs   0.2</p>
<p>    Turnover		    130.41   vs  77.47</p>
<p>Full name - LeisureNet Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The fitness and leisure company, which does not declare interim dividends, said the opening of new Health &amp; Racquet and Foodgro outlets in the second half of the year should enable it to report continued growth for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
